****
Magnesium and Sodium are really odd balls of the spectrum. They show obvious prominences, bright plages, and very dens filaments do show up on the disk. 
Overall, both the Na I D and the Mg I b disk is an anemic variant of a broad band selection of the Ca II K/H region.

Depending on the features on the Sun and fine tuning the aggressivenes 
of the processing algorithm, and of course the always problematic atmospheric seeing conditions, varying details can be shown.
